PLUNGER                                                   CMS Nucleus extension

Use the PLUNGER command to control use of CMS Pipelines.

+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|                                                                             |
| >>--PLUNGER---.--DEBUG--.-------.--.--><                                    |
|               |         +--OFF--+  |                                        |
|               |         '--ON---'  |                                        |
|               +--DISABLE-----------+                                        |
|               +--ENABLE------------+                                        |
|               '--VERSION-----------'                                        |
|                                                                             |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+

where:

DEBUG    on its own specifies to display the current debugging status for
         Plunger.

DEBUG OFF specifies to stop debugging of Plunger.

DEBUG ON  specifies to start debugging of Plunger.

DISABLE  specifies to disable use of CMS Pipelines, and unload Plunger and
         CMS Pipelines from memory.

ENABLE   specifies to load Plunger and CMS Pipelines into memory, and enable
         use of CMS Pipelines.

VERSION specifies to display the version of Plunger in use.

